The RHipe C engine is not running.
Try, under your user name
(a)  rhex(r, mapred=list(mapred.job.tracker='local')) (not sure if this helps much)
(b) Enter the following in a shell script

export rhipe_combiner=0
io.sort.mb=1
REDUCESETUP=""
rhipe_setup_map=""
rhipe_map=""
rhipe_cleanup_map=""
export R_HOME=/ln/meraki/custom/lib64/R  #1
/ln/meraki/custom//lib64/R/library/Rhipe/libs/imperious.so #2

(change the last two lines for your machine:

the
#2 can be got from rhoptions()$runner[1]
#1 from R.home()

Try running this on the cluster compute node (and not just from where you submit the job)
Are the cluster nodes identical?

